According to producer [[Kazuaki Kishida]], planning for a sequel to ''[[Godzilla Minus One]]'' began in late May 2023 after a strong internal reaction at the film's first completed screening for [[Toho]] employees. Director [[Takashi Yamazaki]] subsequently delivered an initial five-page plot outline for ''Godzilla Minus Zero'' shortly before ''Minus One''<nowiki/>'s November 2023 release. Kishida remarked: "Of course, there were some differences from the final version, but the main framework was already in place."<ref name=":7">{{Cite web |title=特撮ばんざい！第77回：１万字インタビュー『ゴジラ-1.0』から『ゴジラ-0.0』へ――岸田一晃プロデューサーが語る、世界を切り拓いたゴジラの現在地 |url=https://www.monomagazine.com/120419 |access-date=September 20, 2026 |website=モノ・マガジンweb |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260913025112/https://www.monomagazine.com/120419 |archive-date=September 13, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Throughout the film's theatrical run, Yamazaki repeatedly told interviewers that no discussions of a sequel had taken place, while sharing ideas he had for one. In 2026, Yamazaki admitted that his earlier claims of "no talks" were untrue and that he had intentionally "planted the seed" for a continuation by hinting at future story directions.<ref>{{cite AV media|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yFRTRpLfOpI|title=Interview with Godzilla: Minus Zero (2026) Director: Takashi Yamazaki|via=YouTube|date=April 25, 2026|access-date=July 13, 2026|time=00:04:39–00:06:10|author=Team JVS|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260713021927/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yFRTRpLfOpI|archive-date=July 13, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> Kishida noted that discussions continued in parallel with the film's promotion and [[Academy Awards|Academy Award]] campaign.<ref name=":7" />

Following the critical and commercial success of ''Godzilla Minus One''—which became one of the [[List of highest-grossing Japanese films|highest-grossing Japanese films of all time]] and won the [[Academy Award for Best Visual Effects]] among its [[List of accolades received by Godzilla Minus One|many accolades]]—Yamazaki was confirmed on November 1, 2024, to helm another ''[[Godzilla (franchise)|Godzilla]]'' film. The announcement was first made during the film's Japanese television broadcast on [[Nippon Television]]'s ''{{Ill|Friday Road Show|ja|金曜ロードショー}}''.<ref>{{Cite web |script-title=ja:ゴジラ新作映画、山崎貴監督・脚本・VFXで製作決定！ : 映画ニュース |url=https://eiga.com/news/20241101/38/ |access-date=November 4, 2025 |script-website=ja:映画.com |language=ja |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241207065218/https://eiga.com/news/20241101/38/ |archive-date=December 7, 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> At that time, Toho did not disclose if it would be a direct sequel to ''Godzilla Minus One'' or a standalone film.<ref name="Gizmodo">{{Cite web |last=Whitbrook |first=James |date=November 1, 2024 |title=Godzilla Minus One's Takashi Yamazaki Is Making Another Godzilla Movie |url=https://gizmodo.com/takashi-yamazaki-godzilla-minus-one-sequel-new-movie-toho-2000519226 |access-date=November 5, 2025 |website=[[Gizmodo]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241103033402/https://gizmodo.com/takashi-yamazaki-godzilla-minus-one-sequel-new-movie-toho-2000519226 |archive-date=November 3, 2024 |url-status=live }}</ref> At the [[23rd Visual Effects Society Awards]] on February 11, 2025, Yamazaki revealed scripting and storyboarding of his follow-up was ongoing and expected a budget higher than that of ''Godzilla Minus One''<nowiki/>'s, which cost less than {{USD|15 million}}.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Giardina |first=Carolyn |date=February 12, 2025 |title='Godzilla Minus One' Director Takashi Yamazaki; 'Here' VFX Pros Weigh In on AI at VES Awards |url=https://variety.com/2025/artisans/news/godzilla-minus-one-director-takashi-yamazaki-ai-ves-awards-1236305429/ |access-date=November 4, 2025 |website=Variety |language=en-US |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260714014456/https://variety.com/2025/artisans/news/godzilla-minus-one-director-takashi-yamazaki-ai-ves-awards-1236305429/ |archive-date=July 14, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>

When planning the sequel, Yamazaki chose [[King Ghidorah]] due to a childhood connection with the character. Born in 1964—the year of the monster's debut in ''[[Ghidorah, the Three-Headed Monster]]'' and the [[Dragon (zodiac)|Year of the Dragon]]—Yamazaki is also from [[Matsumoto, Nagano]], the city attacked by Ghidorah in that film.<ref name="Animate_Times-1">{{Cite web |title=『ゴジラ-0.0』山崎貴監督インタビュー前編 |trans-title=Interview with ''Godzilla Minus Zero'' Director Takashi Yamazaki (Part 1) |url=https://www.animatetimes.com/news/details.php?id=1793061471 |access-date=2026-11-12 |website=Animate Times |language=ja}}</ref> In 1971, after seeing a local flyer advertising a revival screening with the slogan "King Ghidorah attacks Matsumoto!", he attended expecting the destruction of [[Matsumoto Castle]].<ref name="Raineri2026-1">{{Cite web |last=Raineri |first=Sebastien |date=2026-11-10 |title=''Godzilla Minus Zero'' director sees the monster as a mirror |url=https://www.japantimes.co.jp/culture/2026/11/10/film/godzilla-minus-zero-takashi-yamazaki-interview/ |access-date=2026-11-12 |website=[[The Japan Times]] |language=en}}</ref> In the film, however, Ghidorah merely flew over the castle, causing tiles to fall. Disappointed by this, Yamazaki later chose to include the monster in ''Minus Zero'' as a form of personal "revenge", fulfilling a 55-year desire by depicting it damaging the castle.<ref name="Animate_Times-1" /><ref name="Raineri2026-1" />

=== Pre-production ===
In June 2025, the [[Agency for Cultural Affairs]]–commissioned "Film Staff Development Project" disclosed that filming for Yamazaki's next movie would take place from early August to December 2025, and they were seeking film students to recruit.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |script-title=ja:募集中: 山崎貴監督最新作（主な監督作：『ALWAYS 三丁目の夕日 』『永遠の0』『ゴジラ-1.0』） |url=https://cinema-intern.bunka.go.jp/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250618045734/https://cinema-intern.bunka.go.jp/ |archive-date=June 18, 2025 |access-date=November 4, 2025 |website=cinema-intern.bunka.go.jp |publisher=[[Agency for Cultural Affairs]] |language=ja}}</ref> On July 17, [[Bloomberg News]] reported that [[Toho International]]'s president, Kōji Ueda, clarified that the new ''Godzilla'' film would be a sequel and a 2026 release was currently planned.<ref name=":1">{{cite web |last=Kim |first=Sohee |date=July 17, 2025 |title=Godzilla Conquered Japan. Now Its Owner Plots a Global Takeover |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2025-07-17/godzilla-studio-toho-plans-more-films-sequels-anime-and-jujutsu-kaisen |url-access=subscription |access-date=November 4, 2025 |website=[[Bloomberg News]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250826094855/https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2025-07-17/godzilla-studio-toho-plans-more-films-sequels-anime-and-jujutsu-kaisen |archive-date=August 26, 2025 |url-status=live }}</ref> On July 27, the site yamazakimovie-extra.jp<ref>{{Cite web |title=福袋研究所｜テンプレ |url=https://yamazakimovie-extra.jp/ |access-date=2026-11-12 |website=福袋研究所 |language=ja}}</ref> was launched to find volunteer extras for the film from August to September. It recycled the {{Nihongo|''Blockbuster Monster Movie'' (temp)|超大作怪獣映画(仮)|lead=yes}} [[Working title|placeholder]] used for ''Minus One'' during pre-production and confirmed Toho would be financing with [[Robot Communications]], featuring an all-star Japanese cast.<ref name="Extra">{{cite web |script-title=ja:東宝新作映画『超大作怪獣映画（仮）』最新作 ボランティアエキストラさん大募集!! |trans-title=Toho's Latest Film ''Blockbuster Monster Movie'' (Tentative): Huge Recruitment of Volunteer Extras!! |url=https://yamazakimovie-extra.jp/ |accessdate=November 4, 2025 |work=yamazakimovie-extra.jp |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251205230137/http://yamazakimovie-extra.jp/ |archive-date=December 5, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

=== Filming ===
[[Principal photography]] took place with extras on location in [[Ibaraki Prefecture]] from August 30 to September 14, 2025.<ref name="Extra" /> ''[[The Hollywood Reporter]]'' claimed additional shooting took place in New Zealand and Norway.<ref name=":2">{{Cite web |last=Brzeski |first=Patrick |date=November 3, 2025 |title=Japan's Toho Studios Reveals Title for Next Godzilla Movie |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/japan-toho-studios-title-godzilla-minus-zero-1236416477/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251103063658/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/japan-toho-studios-title-godzilla-minus-zero-1236416477/ |archive-date=November 3, 2025 |access-date=November 4, 2025 |website=The Hollywood Reporter |language=en-US}}</ref> However, according to an official [[press release]], the film was shot entirely in Japan.<ref>{{Cite web |date=July 9, 2026 |title=TOHO AND GKIDS Reveal New Poster And Teaser For GODZILLA MINUS ZERO |url=https://gkids.com/2026/07/09/toho-and-gkids-reveal-new-poster-and-teaser-for-godzilla-minus-zero/ |access-date=July 12, 2026 |website=[[GKIDS]] |language=en-US |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260712092942/https://gkids.com/2026/07/09/toho-and-gkids-reveal-new-poster-and-teaser-for-godzilla-minus-zero/ |archive-date=July 12, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=TOHO And GKIDS Reveal New Poster And Teaser For GODZILLA MINUS ZERO |url=https://www.scifijapan.com/godzilla-toho/toho-and-gkids-reveal-new-poster-and-teaser-for-godzilla-minus-zero |access-date=July 12, 2026 |website=SciFi Japan |language=en-gb |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260714004356/https://www.scifijapan.com/godzilla-toho/toho-and-gkids-reveal-new-poster-and-teaser-for-godzilla-minus-zero |archive-date=July 14, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> Filming was expected to wrap in late December.<ref name=":0" /> It became the first Japanese production [[List of IMAX films|filmed for IMAX]].<ref name="Moreau">{{Cite web |last=Moreau |first=Jordan |date=April 14, 2026 |title=''Godzilla Minus Zero'' Trailer Brings the Kaiju to New York City; Director Reveals First Plot Details and Imax Release |url=https://variety.com/2026/film/news/godzilla-minus-zero-trailer-new-york-1236712354/ |access-date=April 14, 2026 |website=Variety |language=en-US |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260414164839/https://variety.com/2026/film/news/godzilla-minus-zero-trailer-new-york-1236712354/ |archive-date=April 14, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> Yamazaki's longtime collaborator [[Kōzō Shibasaki]] served as cinematographer.<ref name="Ibaraki"/>

Extra recruitment reports also state that due to the film's [[historical drama]] setting, there would be restrictions on the extras' costume sizes, hairstyles, and hair colors (with hair dyeing being prohibited) for those participating as extras. A scene featuring Japanese maintenance soldiers was shot at a temple in [[Maizuru]] on November 3, which was Godzilla Day in Japan.<ref>{{Cite web |script-title=ja:【１１月３日(月)京都府・舞鶴泉源寺にて★予備日】東宝新作映画『超大作怪獣映画(仮)』最新作よりエキストラ募集 {{!}} エキストラ募集・エキストラ情報｜EKISUTORA.INFO｜株式会社トループ |url=https://ekisutora.info/%E5%B1%B1%E5%B4%8E%E8%B2%B4%E7%9B%A3%E7%9D%A3%E3%80%8E%E8%B6%85%E5%A4%A7%E4%BD%9C%E6%80%AA%E7%8D%A3%E6%98%A0%E7%94%BB%EF%BC%88%E4%BB%AE%EF%BC%89%E3%80%8F/20251103 |access-date=November 19, 2025 |website=ekisutora.info |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251011010928/https://ekisutora.info/%E5%B1%B1%E5%B4%8E%E8%B2%B4%E7%9B%A3%E7%9D%A3%E3%80%8E%E8%B6%85%E5%A4%A7%E4%BD%9C%E6%80%AA%E7%8D%A3%E6%98%A0%E7%94%BB%EF%BC%88%E4%BB%AE%EF%BC%89%E3%80%8F/20251103 |archive-date=October 11, 2025 |url-status=dead}}</ref> Filming occurred around [[Seijōgakuen-mae Station]] on November 25,<ref>{{Cite web |script-title=ja:山崎貴監督『超大作怪獣映画（仮）』 {{!}} エキストラ募集・エキストラ情報｜EKISUTORA.INFO｜株式会社トループ |url=https://ekisutora.info/taxonomy/term/1122 |access-date=November 4, 2025 |website=ekisutora.info |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251011003120/https://ekisutora.info/taxonomy/term/1122 |archive-date=October 11, 2025 |url-status=dead}}</ref> and in [[Inashiki District, Ibaraki]] on December 15.<ref>{{Cite web|script-title=ja:【１２月１５日(月)茨城県・稲敷郡にて】東宝新作映画『超大作怪獣映画(仮)』最新作よりエキストラ募集 {{!}} エキストラ募集・エキストラ情報｜EKISUTORA.INFO｜株式会社トループ|url=https://ekisutora.info/%E5%B1%B1%E5%B4%8E%E8%B2%B4%E7%9B%A3%E7%9D%A3%E3%80%8E%E8%B6%85%E5%A4%A7%E4%BD%9C%E6%80%AA%E7%8D%A3%E6%98%A0%E7%94%BB%EF%BC%88%E4%BB%AE%EF%BC%89%E3%80%8F/20251215|website=ekisutora.info|access-date=November 27, 2025}} {{Dead link|date=November 2026 |bot=InternetArchiveBot }}</ref>

The film had a roughly 30% budget increase over its predecessor, according to Yamazaki.<ref name="Filmmaker"/> On March 16, 2026, Yamazaki attended a joint government–industry meeting under Japan's Intellectual Property Strategy Headquarters, which addressed working conditions in the content industry. Discussing his experience on ''Minus Zero'', he said the new Eiteki certification system reduced crew exhaustion during filming and improved working conditions, allowing more humane lives for production staff who previously endured extremely harsh schedules, but its rigid daily time limits sometimes forced production to stop even when additional shooting would have helped.<ref>{{cite web |date=March 16, 2026 |title=第１回コンテンツ戦略ワーキンググループ／第１回クリエイティブ戦略タスクフォース合同会議 議事要旨 |trans-title=Minutes of the 1st Content Strategy Working Group / 1st Creative Strategy Task Force Joint Meeting |url=https://www.cas.go.jp/jp/seisakukaigi/titeki2/tyousakai/kousou/contentswg/dai1/gijiyoshi.pdf |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261019023417/https://www.cas.go.jp/jp/seisakukaigi/titeki2/tyousakai/kousou/contentswg/dai1/gijiyoshi.pdf |archive-date=October 19, 2026 |access-date= |publisher=[[Cabinet Secretariat (Japan)|Cabinet Secretariat]] |language=ja |url-status=live}}</ref>

At the opening ceremony of Godzilla Fest 2025, held on November 3, 2025, at the [[Tokyo Dome City Hall]], Toho unveiled the official title of Yamazaki's next Godzilla feature as ''Godzilla Minus Zero''.<ref name=":2" /> A teaser logo, personally illustrated by Yamazaki, was shown.<ref name=":2" /> Yamazaki said via a pre-recorded message that he was unable to attend the festival since he is currently filming ''Minus Zero''.<ref name=":3">{{Cite web |date=November 3, 2025 |title=''Godzilla Minus Zero'' Title Reveal Ignites Fans at Godzilla Fest 2025 |url=https://godzilla.com/blogs/news/godzilla-minus-zero-title-reveal-ignites-fans-at-godzilla-fest-2025 |access-date=November 5, 2025 |website=Godzilla.com |publisher=[[Toho International]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260103171118/https://godzilla.com/blogs/news/godzilla-minus-zero-title-reveal-ignites-fans-at-godzilla-fest-2025 |archive-date=January 3, 2026 |url-status=live }}</ref> It was also announced that [[Shirogumi]] will handle VFX; and production is shared between [[Toho Studios]] and Robot Communications.<ref>{{Cite web |date=November 3, 2025 |title=Godzilla Minus Zero - News Roundup |url=https://www.tohokingdom.com/blog/godzilla-minus-zero-news-roundup/ |access-date=November 4, 2025 |website=Toho Kingdom |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251120214800/https://www.tohokingdom.com/blog/godzilla-minus-zero-news-roundup/ |archive-date=November 20, 2025 |url-status=live }}</ref> Industry sources told ''The Hollywood Reporter'' the same day that "the new film is being positioned not just as a sequel but as a statement piece".<ref name=":2" /> Plot details, cast confirmations, and an exact premiere date remained undisclosed.<ref name=":2" /><ref name=":3" />

On December 10, Yamazaki finished that day's filming at 5:00 p.m. and then made a surprise appearance at a Tokyo event for [[James Cameron]]'s ''[[Avatar: Fire and Ash]]''. During their onstage conversation, Cameron expressed enthusiasm for ''Godzilla Minus Zero'' and jokingly offered to direct the film's second unit if it fell behind schedule.<ref>{{Cite web |date=December 10, 2025 |editor-last=Shoji |editor-first=Satoru |title=James Cameron Tells Godzilla Director Takashi Yamazaki "I'll Come Help You" |url=https://us.oricon-group.com/news/7144/ |access-date=December 11, 2025 |website=[[Oricon]] |language=en-US |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251211053815/https://us.oricon-group.com/news/7144/ |archive-date=December 11, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

===Post-production===
{{See also|Godzilla Minus Zero (soundtrack){{!}}''Godzilla Minus Zero'' (soundtrack)}}
The film's poster credits three visual effects supervisors: [[Kiyoko Shibuya]], previously the visual effects director on ''Minus One'', Takayuki Ueki, and Eishin Okubo. Takashi Yamazaki again receives the "VFX by" credit.<ref name="Ibaraki">{{Cite tweet|author=Ibaraki Film Commission Official |language=ja |user=ibarakiken_fc|number=2097886152875499632|title=11月3日（火・祝）に公開予定の『ゴジラｰ0.0』 なんと、前作『ゴジラｰ1.0』に続き、茨城県内で撮影が行われました！ どんなシーンに登場するのかお楽しみに✨ 映画とのタイアップ企画も進行中⁉続報をお待ちください☺|date=September 10, 2026 |access-date=September 20, 2026 }}</ref> Other returning longtime collaborators include editor [[Ryūji Miyajima]]<ref name="Ibaraki"/><ref>{{Cite web |last=Shida |first=Ayaka |date=May 23, 2026 |script-title=ja:映画編集者・宮島竜治氏による映像編集ワークショップおよび特別公開講座を開催します |trans-title=We will be holding a video editing workshop and a special public lecture by film editor Ryūji Miyajima. |url=https://www.hi-tech.ac.jp/entry/51885 |access-date=July 6, 2026 |publisher=[[Hachinohe Institute of Technology]] |language=ja |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260706082122/https://www.hi-tech.ac.jp/entry/51885 |archive-date=July 6, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> and composer [[Naoki Satō]].<ref name="Ibaraki"/><ref name=":10">{{Cite web |title=''Godzilla Minus Zero'' Japanese Press Release -- Direct From Toho! |url=https://www.scifijapan.com/articles/godzilla-minus-zero-japanese-press-release-direct-from-toho |access-date=July 11, 2026 |website=[[SciFi Japan]] |language=en-gb |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260712034552/https://www.scifijapan.com/articles/godzilla-minus-zero-japanese-press-release-direct-from-toho |archive-date=July 12, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Shirogumi again handled the visual effects, continuing its work from ''Minus One''. Yamazaki said that the larger budget provided by Toho compared to the previous film allowed him to expand the effects team, but that the production had also "moved the goalposts" on what the shots were expected to achieve. He stated that the sequel would contain more effects cuts than ''Minus One'' and that each effects shot was more complex than those in that film.<ref name="Collider">{{Cite web |last1=Jones |first1=Tamera |last2=Weintraub |first2=Steven |date=April 15, 2026 |title=''Godzilla Minus Zero'' Is Directly Inspired By Steven Spielberg and The Greatest Sci-Fi Directors Ever [Exclusive] |url=https://collider.com/godzilla-minus-zero-imax-scenes-vfx-shots-james-cameron-steven-spielberg-inspiration-takashi-yamazaki-interview/ |access-date=April 16, 2026 |website=[[Collider (website)|Collider]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260416154625/https://collider.com/godzilla-minus-zero-imax-scenes-vfx-shots-james-cameron-steven-spielberg-inspiration-takashi-yamazaki-interview/ |archive-date=April 16, 2026 |url-status=live }}</ref>

The visual effects team expanded to around 50 on ''Minus Zero'', gaining around 15 new members since ''Minus One''.<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 18, 2026 |title=Takashi Yamasaki, director de 'Godzilla Minus Zero': "Sentí que la pantalla no aguantaría" |trans-title=Takashi Yamazaki, director of ''Godzilla Minus Zero'': "I felt the screen wouldn't be able to take it" |url=https://www.elespectador.com/revista-vea/peliculas-series-y-novelas/takashi-yamasaki-director-de-godzilla-minus-zero-senti-que-la-pantalla-no-aguantaria/ |access-date=November 8, 2026 |website=[[El Espectador]] |language=spanish |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261030220626/https://www.elespectador.com/revista-vea/peliculas-series-y-novelas/takashi-yamasaki-director-de-godzilla-minus-zero-senti-que-la-pantalla-no-aguantaria/ |archive-date=October 30, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> Notably, Yamazaki recruited CG animator [[Atsushi Sato (animator)|Atsushi Sato]]—a veteran of Hollywood productions—from semi-retirement to supervise key animation, especially King Ghidorah and its physical interactions with Godzilla. Yamazaki credited Sato's work on the large-scale combat sequences and, in particular, the climactic battle amid the ruins of Ginza, which he called the most difficult scene because of the challenge of depicting the two kaiju tangling and colliding convincingly without model clipping. For Ghidorah's design, Yamazaki sought a "god bird" appearance, giving the creature an especially long tail with a curtain-like element and drawing on Sato's experience animating dragons to achieve natural aerial movement.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Desowitz |first=Bill |date=November 7, 2026 |title=How ''Godzilla Minus Zero'' unleashed King Ghidorah: 'A whole different kind of fear,' says director Takashi Yamazaki |url=https://www.goldderby.com/film/2026/godzilla-minus-zero-explained-takashi-yamazaki-interview-king-ghidorah-vfx/ |access-date=November 8, 2026 |website=Gold Derby |language=en-US}}</ref>

While promoting the film in April 2026, Yamazaki reported that the Japanese team was sending him shots daily and that a rough assembly of the film already existed, though production remained "deep in VFX land". After reviewing one in-progress sequence that morning, he described it as "probably one of the best kaiju sequences that I've ever seen" and said even the unfinished version had given him goosebumps, adding that audiences would "see something they've never seen before".<ref name="Collider"/>

Yamazaki said the visual effect shot of Godzilla appearing near the [[Statue of Liberty]] was inspired by the shot in ''[[Cloverfield]]'' (2008) wherein [[Clover (creature)|its monster]] throws the statue's severed head.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Alter |first=Ethan |date=April 15, 2026 |title=''Godzilla Minus Zero'' director credits 'Cloverfield' for that bonkers Statue of Liberty trailer cameo |url=https://www.goldderby.com/film/2026/godzilla-minus-zero-takashi-yamazaki-cloverfield/ |access-date=September 29, 2026 |website=Gold Derby |language=en-US |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261009185147/https://www.goldderby.com/film/2026/godzilla-minus-zero-takashi-yamazaki-cloverfield/ |archive-date=October 9, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> He also named ''Cloverfield'' when asked for his favorite [[Statue of Liberty in popular culture#Film|Statue of Liberty appearance in genre cinema]], and framed the image of "smashing or doing something with the Statue of Liberty" as a VFX-industry "bucket list" shot.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Vejvoda |first=Jim |date=April 17, 2026 |title=Audiences Will "Feel What It's Like to be Chased by Godzilla" in Minus Zero |url=https://www.ign.com/articles/godzilla-minus-zero-will-bring-a-whole-new-level-of-terror-director-reveals |access-date=September 29, 2026 |website=IGN |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261010035915/https://www.ign.com/articles/godzilla-minus-zero-will-bring-a-whole-new-level-of-terror-director-reveals |archive-date=October 10, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>
== Release ==
===Marketing and promotion===
On March 9, 2026, it was announced that footage from the film would be shown at [[CinemaCon]] at [[the Colosseum at Caesars Palace]] on April 14, with Yamazaki presenting.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://variety.com/2026/film/news/godzilla-minus-zero-first-look-cinemacon-1236682682/|title=''Godzilla Minus Zero'' First Look Set for CinemaCon as Takashi Yamazaki Joins GKIDS Presentation|website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|date=March 9, 2026|last=French|access-date=March 14, 2026|first=Kennedy|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260820085616/https://variety.com/2026/film/news/godzilla-minus-zero-first-look-cinemacon-1236682682/|archive-date=August 20, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> The teaser trailer released later that same day. Behind the scenes footage was also shown at CinemaCon.<ref name=":6">{{cite magazine |last=Stenzel |first=Wesley |date=April 14, 2026 |title=The biggest news from CinemaCon day 2: First ''Godzilla Minus Zero'' footage, Neon's buzzy slate, and more |url=https://ew.com/biggest-news-cinemacon-day-2-godzilla-minus-zero-more-11949801 |access-date=April 15, 2026 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260415034117/https://ew.com/biggest-news-cinemacon-day-2-godzilla-minus-zero-more-11949801 |archive-date=April 15, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> An unidentified actor provided voiceover as an American military member in the teaser;<ref name=":6" /> it was later revealed to be the voice of newcomer Wes Wing, who would subsequently attend the annual [[fan convention]] [[G-Fest]] as a guest.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Wes Wing |url=https://www.g-festcon.com/guests/wes-wing |access-date=September 20, 2026 |website=[[G-Fest]] |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260920051933/https://www.g-festcon.com/guests/wes-wing |archive-date=September 20, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> A second teaser premiered on July 9.<ref name=":9" /> A further trailer was released on September 8 in 1.43:1 IMAX format, revealing the presence of [[King Ghidorah]] in the film.<ref>{{cite web |title=GODZILLA MINUS ZERO Official Trailer From TOHO and GKIDS |url=https://www.scifijapan.com/godzilla-toho/godzilla-minus-zero-trailer |website=SciFi Japan |access-date=September 8, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260909043915/https://www.scifijapan.com/godzilla-toho/godzilla-minus-zero-trailer |archive-date=September 9, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>

On August 16, 2026, ''Godzilla Minus Zero'' collaborated with the [[Ban'ei Kinen]] at [[Obihiro]] Racecourse. The event featured a Godzilla panel exhibition, a Godzilla statue, an appearance by the film's producer Kazuaki Kishida, and collaboration merchandise, including a limited-edition T-shirt, offered as a prize.<ref>{{Cite web |script-title=ja:「第38回ばんえいグランプリ」ファン投票 7/20(月)まで！ |url=https://www.banei-keiba.or.jp/ed_detail.php?id=1628 |access-date=July 9, 2026 |website=[[Ban'ei Kinen]] |language=ja |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260720082520/https://www.banei-keiba.or.jp/ed_detail.php?id=1628 |archive-date=July 20, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> In July, the [[Los Angeles Dodgers]] and Toho announced "''Godzilla Minus Zero'' Night" at [[Dodger Stadium]]. It took place on September 24, during a game against the [[San Diego Padres]]. The first 40,000 fans in attendance received an exclusive Godzilla bobblehead, and the evening featured a large-scale [[drone show]] with Godzilla-themed visuals.<ref>{{Cite web |date=July 16, 2026 |title=Los Angeles Dodgers Announce Godzilla Minus Zero Night at Dodger Stadi |url=https://godzilla.com/blogs/news/los-angeles-dodgers-announce-godzilla-minus-zero-night-at-dodger-stadium |access-date=July 25, 2026 |website=Godzilla.com |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260905104809/https://godzilla.com/blogs/news/los-angeles-dodgers-announce-godzilla-minus-zero-night-at-dodger-stadium |archive-date=September 5, 2026 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Gajewski |first=Ryan |date=September 29, 2026 |title='Godzilla Minus Zero': Dodgers Giveaway Draws Lines for Final Home Game |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/local-news/godzilla-minus-zero-dodgers-giveaway-lines-final-home-game-1236714124/ |access-date=September 29, 2026 |website=The Hollywood Reporter |language=en-US |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260929225000/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/local-news/godzilla-minus-zero-dodgers-giveaway-lines-final-home-game-1236714124/ |archive-date=September 29, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> The film's marketing costs for the United States and Canada came in under $10 million.<ref name="Alessandro2026-1" />

The final trailer for the film premiered during the ''Minus One'' re-release in selected Japanese theaters on October 8, 2026.<ref>{{Cite web |title=福岡市 博多 映画 キャナルシティ博多 『『ゴジラ-1.0』IMAX復活上映 & 5大都市生中継【-1.0→-0.0 ナイト】（ワンゼロナイト）』 スケジュール ユナイテッド・シネマ |url=https://www.unitedcinemas.jp/canalcity/film.php?movie=14135&from=fb |access-date=September 30, 2026 |website=ローソン・ユナイテッドシネマ,ユナイテッド･シネマ映画館 |language=ja|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260930202654/https://www.unitedcinemas.jp/canalcity/film.php?movie=14135&from=film|archive-date=September 30, 2026|url-status=dead}}</ref>

=== Theatrical ===
''Godzilla Minus Zero'' premiered at the [[2026 New York Film Festival]] on September 26, 2026,<ref>{{Cite web |title=World Premiere of Takashi Yamazaki's Godzilla Minus Zero Is 64th New York Film Festival Spotlight Gala |url=https://www.filmlinc.org/nyff2026/daily/world-premiere-of-takashi-yamazakis-godzilla-minus-zero-is-64th-new-york-film-festival-spotlight-gala/ |access-date=August 4, 2026 |website=Film at Lincoln Center |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260927040352/https://www.filmlinc.org/nyff2026/daily/world-premiere-of-takashi-yamazakis-godzilla-minus-zero-is-64th-new-york-film-festival-spotlight-gala/ |archive-date=September 27, 2026 |url-status=live }}</ref> and was also set to be the Centerpiece screening at the [[39th Tokyo International Film Festival]] on November 1, 2026.<ref name="var">{{Cite news |url=https://variety.com/2026/film/news/godzilla-minus-zero-tokyo-centerpiece-sukiyaki-colony-1236847173/ |title=''Godzilla Minus Zero'' Named Centerpiece of Tokyo Film Festival as 'Sukiyaki' Opens, 'Colony' Closes |author=Naman Ramachandran |work=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |date=September 1, 2026 |access-date=September 2, 2026 |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260913042116/https://variety.com/2026/film/news/godzilla-minus-zero-tokyo-centerpiece-sukiyaki-colony-1236847173/ |archive-date=September 13, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> It released in Japan on November 3, 2026, and North America on November 6, 2026, coinciding with ''[[Ramayana: Part 1]]'' and [[The Cat in the Hat (2026 film)|''The Cat in the Hat'']],<ref name="DeadlineRelease">{{cite news|title=''Godzilla Minus Zero'' Sets Fall Theatrical Release|last=D'Alessandro|first=Anthony|url=https://deadline.com/2026/01/godzilla-minus-zero-release-date-1236678267/|work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|date=January 9, 2026|access-date=January 9, 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260114220706/https://deadline.com/2026/01/godzilla-minus-zero-release-date-1236678267/|archive-date=January 14, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="HR">{{cite web|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/godzilla-minus-zero-set-for-november-release-1236469084/|title=''Godzilla Minus Zero'' Sets November Release in Theaters|website=Hollywood Reporter|date=January 9, 2026|last=Couch|first=Aaron|access-date=January 10, 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260110010653/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/godzilla-minus-zero-set-for-november-release-1236469084/|archive-date=January 10, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> also in [[IMAX]].<ref name="Moreau" /> This timing adheres to the longstanding Toho–[[Legendary Entertainment|Legendary Pictures]] agreement that prohibits competing ''Godzilla'' films from releasing in the same calendar year, as previously seen with ''Godzilla Minus One'' (2023) and ''[[Godzilla x Kong: The New Empire]]'' (2024). Legendary's next [[Monsterverse]] entry, [[Godzilla x Kong: Supernova|''Godzilla x Kong: Supernov''a]], is set for 2027.<ref name=":5">{{Cite web |last=Nelson |first=Samantha |date=November 3, 2025 |title=The sequel to Godzilla Minus One gets title and release window |url=https://www.polygon.com/godzilla-minus-zero-announced-sequel/ |access-date=November 19, 2025 |website=[[Polygon (website)|Polygon]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251125175204/https://www.polygon.com/godzilla-minus-zero-announced-sequel/ |archive-date=November 25, 2025 |url-status=live }}</ref>

On January 9, 2026, the film was announced to be distributed by Toho's subsidiary [[GKIDS]] in North American theatres on November 6, 2026, three days after its Japanese release date on November 3, 2026.<ref name="HR" /><ref name="DeadlineRelease" /> Select IMAX theaters in the United States, United Kingdom, and Mexico also had early access showings on November 3 to celebrate Godzilla Day.<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 7, 2026 |title=''Godzilla Minus Zero'' Movie Theatre Concessions Revealed: Popcorn Bucket |url=https://godzilla.com/blogs/news/godzilla-minus-zero-movie-theatre-concessions-revealed-popcorn-buckets-cups-and-more |access-date=October 15, 2026 |website=Godzilla.com |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261014052209/https://godzilla.com/blogs/news/godzilla-minus-zero-movie-theatre-concessions-revealed-popcorn-buckets-cups-and-more |archive-date=October 14, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=September 9, 2026 |title=''Godzilla Minus Zero'' Will Be Released in UK IMAX Cinemas From November 3 |url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2026-09-09/godzilla-minus-zero-will-be-released-in-uk-imax-cinemas-from-november-3/.241556 |access-date=October 15, 2026 |website=[[Anime News Network]] |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261016125655/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2026-09-09/godzilla-minus-zero-will-be-released-in-uk-imax-cinemas-from-november-3/.241556 |archive-date=October 16, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=GODZILLA MINUS ZERO Mexican Release Details From Corazón Films |url=https://www.scifijapan.com/godzilla-toho/godzilla-minus-zero-mexican-release-details-from-corazon-films |access-date=October 15, 2026 |website=[[SciFi Japan]] |language=en-gb |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261015221422/https://www.scifijapan.com/godzilla-toho/godzilla-minus-zero-mexican-release-details-from-corazon-films |archive-date=October 15, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> Notably, ''Minus Zero'' is the first ''Godzilla'' film to receive an R rating from the [[Motion Picture Association]] for its United States release, namely for "some violent content/bloody images".<ref>{{Cite web |last= |first= |date=September 24, 2026 |title="Godzilla Minus Zero" Scores An R Rating |url=https://www.darkhorizons.com/godzilla-minus-zero-scores-an-r-rating/ |access-date=September 22, 2026 |website=Dark Horizons |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260923032234/https://www.darkhorizons.com/godzilla-minus-zero-scores-an-r-rating/ |archive-date=September 23, 2026 |url-status=live }}</ref>

== Reception ==

=== Box office ===
''Godzilla Minus Zero'' has grossed $33.3 million ({{JPY|5.3 billion}}) in Japan, $54.7 million in the United States and Canada, and $32.5 million in other territories for a worldwide total of $120.5 million.<ref name="CinemaToday"/><ref name="BOM">{{Cite Box Office Mojo |id=34384661 |title=Godzilla Minus Zero |access-date=November 23, 2026 }}</ref><ref name="Numbers">{{Cite web |url=https://www.the-numbers.com/movie/Godzilla-Minus-Zero-(2026-Japan) |title=''Godzilla Minus Zero'' (ゴジラ-0.0) |website=[[The Numbers (website)|The Numbers]] |access-date=November 14, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261108160407/https://www.the-numbers.com/movie/Godzilla-Minus-Zero-(2026-Japan) |archive-date=November 8, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Deadline">{{cite web |last=D'Alessandro |first=Anthony |title=Johnny Depp's ''Ebenezer'' Richer Abroad At $42M WW; ''Ramayana'' Nears $150M WW; ''Godzilla Minus Zero'' Roars Past $100M WW; ''Wildwood'' $70M – Global Box Office |url=https://deadline.com/2026/11/box-office-global-ebenezer-ramayana-godzilla-minus-zero-1237224479/ |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |date=November 15, 2026 |access-date=November 15, 2026}}</ref>

The film opened in Japan on November 3, 2026, across 448 theatres (including 65 IMAX). It earned ¥910 million (approximately US$5.7 million) and drew over 590,000 attendees on its opening day. This set a record as the highest opening-day gross for any live-action film in Japanese history (Japanese or foreign). It represented 201% of the opening-day gross of its predecessor ''Godzilla Minus One'' (¥452.34 million). Reports noted that the single-day figure approached the first three-day total of ''Minus One'' and positioned the film to potentially become the first ''Godzilla'' entry to surpass ¥10 billion ($63.2 million) at the Japanese box office (''Minus One'' finished at roughly ¥7.65 billion).<ref name="映画.com-1">{{Cite web |title=「ゴジラ－0.0」初日興行収入"実写映画歴代1位"を記録！興収100億円超を狙える大ヒットスタートに : 映画ニュース |url=https://eiga.com/news/20261104/15/ |access-date=November 4, 2026 |website=[[Eiga.com]] |language=ja |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261105020340/https://eiga.com/news/20261104/15 |archive-date=November 5, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="MANTANWEB（まんたんウェブ）2026-1">{{Cite web |date=November 4, 2026 |title=ゴジラ-0.0：初日興収9.1億円、動員59万人を突破 実写映画の日本歴代1位の快挙 100億円突破を狙える好発進 |url=https://mantan-web.jp/article/20261104dog00m200046000a.html |access-date=November 4, 2026 |website=MANTANWEB |language=ja-JP}}</ref><ref name="Alessandro2026-1" />

In the United States and Canada, the film was projected to gross $25–30 million from 3,250 theaters in its opening weekend.<ref name="Alessandro2026-1"/> The film made $14.7 million on its first day, including $6.7 million from previews ($2 million of which from Tuesday's Godzilla Day screenings).<ref name="Deadline-Opening">{{cite web|title=Godzilla Minus Zero' Is A Box Office Hero With $32M Live-Action Foreign-Language Opening Record – Saturday AM Update|url=https://deadline.com/2026/11/box-office-godzilla-minus-zero-cat-in-the-hat-1237215161/|last=Alessandro|first=Anthony|date=November 6, 2026|access-date=November 7, 2026|url-status=live|website=Deadline|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261106173730/https://deadline.com/2026/11/box-office-godzilla-minus-zero-cat-in-the-hat-1237215161/|archive-date=November 6, 2026}}</ref> Its previews became the largest for a GKIDS release in the United States and Canada.<ref name="Alessandro2026-1"/> It went on to debut to $30.6 million, topping the box office. Among its box office records, it recorded the highest opening weekend for a live-action foreign-language film in the U.S. and Canada, and the largest [[IMAX]] global opening for a Japanese film, with $21.3 million of its gross coming from IMAX theaters.<ref name="Alessandro2026-1">{{Cite web |last=D'Alessandro |first=Anthony |date=November 8, 2026 |title=Box Office: ''Godzilla Minus Zero'' Roars Toward Record Opening |url=https://deadline.com/2026/11/box-office-godzilla-minus-zero-cat-in-the-hat-1237215161/ |access-date=November 8, 2026 |website=Deadline |language=en-US |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261106173730/https://deadline.com/2026/11/box-office-godzilla-minus-zero-cat-in-the-hat-1237215161/ |archive-date=November 6, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=D'Alessandro |first=Anthony |date=November 8, 2026 |title=Box Office Global: ''Godzilla Minus Zero'' Beats ''Ramayana'' $63M to $55M WW |url=https://deadline.com/2026/11/box-office-global-godzilla-minus-zero-ramayana-rise-of-a-legend-1237216698/ |access-date=November 8, 2026 |website=Deadline |language=en-US |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261109045303/https://deadline.com/2026/11/box-office-global-godzilla-minus-zero-ramayana-rise-of-a-legend-1237216698/ |archive-date=November 9, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>

During the film's second week of its release, its box office numbers plummeted by roughly 72.2%, making it the steepest sophomore weekend drop in the franchise's history. This resulted in the film being removed from 1,139 out of the 3,250 North American theaters on November 20, 2026.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Faruque |first=Omar |date=Nov 23, 2026 |title=Movieweb.com |url=https://movieweb.com/godzilla-minus-zero-box-office-loss/ |website=MOVIEWEB |publisher=Omar Faruque}}</ref> 

=== Critical response ===
{{Metacritic breakdown|positive=34|mixed=10|negative=0}}
After its [[New York Film Festival]] premiere, reviewers described the film as larger in scope, bolder, and more visually impressive than ''Minus One'', with debate over whether it was better overall than its predecessor.<ref name="RT"/> {{Rotten Tomatoes prose|90|7.8|221|Keeping its epic action rooted in human interest, ''Godzilla Minus Zero'' solidifies director Takashi Yamazaki's take on the King of Monsters as one of the mightiest yet by upping the ante without losing sight of its lovable characters.|ref=yes|access-date=November 22, 2026}} [[Metacritic]], which uses a [[Weighted arithmetic mean|weighted average]], assigned the film a score of 74 out of 100, based on 44 critics, indicating "generally favorable" reviews.<ref name="Metacritic">{{cite web |title=''Godzilla Minus Zero'' |url=https://www.metacritic.com/movie/godzilla-minus-zero/ |website=[[Metacritic]] |publisher=[[Fandom (website)#Fandom, Inc.|Fandom, Inc.]] |access-date=November 7, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260927103703/https://www.metacritic.com/movie/godzilla-minus-zero/ |archive-date=September 27, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> Audiences polled by [[CinemaScore]] gave the film an average grade of "A" on an A+ to F scale, the same grade earned by its predecessor, while 95% of those polled by [[PostTrak]] gave the film a positive score, with 85% saying they would definitely recommend it.<ref name=Deadline-Opening/>

[[Owen Gleiberman]] and Molly Edwards of ''[[Total Film]]'' were among the most enthusiastic critics, describing the sequel as grander and more affecting, and Edwards called it among the strongest films of the year.<ref name=":11">{{Cite web |date=September 27, 2026 |title=Godzilla Minus Zero review: "Easily one of the best films of the year" |url=https://www.gamesradar.com/entertainment/sci-fi-movies/godzilla-minus-zero-review/ |access-date=September 27, 2026 |website=GamesRadar+ |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260927040853/https://www.gamesradar.com/entertainment/sci-fi-movies/godzilla-minus-zero-review/ |archive-date=September 27, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name=":13">{{Cite web |last=Gleiberman |first=Owen |date=September 27, 2026 |title=''Godzilla Minus Zero'' Review: Godzilla and King Ghidorah Battle to the Death in the Even Grander Follow-Up to 'Godzilla Minus One' |url=https://variety.com/2026/film/reviews/godzilla-minus-zero-review-takashi-yamazaki-nyff-1236876075/ |access-date=September 27, 2026 |website=Variety |language=en-US |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260928041140/https://variety.com/2026/film/reviews/godzilla-minus-zero-review-takashi-yamazaki-nyff-1236876075/ |archive-date=September 28, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> David Rooney of ''[[The Hollywood Reporter]]'' called it "a crackling ''kaiju'' [[Epic film|epic]] every bit as exciting as its predecessor", highlighting "some of the most impressively seamless integration of major-scale CGI in recent memory" and Yamazaki's ability to keep the human drama "no less compelling than the monster faceoffs" as well as its set pieces.<ref name=":12">{{Cite web |last=Rooney |first=David |date=September 27, 2026 |title=''Godzilla Minus Zero'' Review: Monster Movie Genius Takashi Yamazaki Returns With a Crackling Kaiju Epic Every Bit as Exciting as Its Predecessor |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-reviews/godzilla-minus-zero-review-takashi-yamazaki-1236712678/ |access-date=September 27, 2026 |website=The Hollywood Reporter |language=en-US |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260929080038/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-reviews/godzilla-minus-zero-review-takashi-yamazaki-1236712678/ |archive-date=September 29, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> Jesse Hassenger, writing in ''[[The Guardian]]'', commended the film for combining [[Disaster film|disaster-movie]] scope with [[Horror film|horror-movie]] intensity while still favoring quality of effects over quantity.<ref name=":32">{{Cite news |last=Hassenger |first=Jesse |date=September 27, 2026 |title=Godzilla Minus Zero review – spectacular Japanese action continues franchise's winning streak |url=https://www.theguardian.com/film/2026/sep/26/godzilla-minus-zero-review-new-york-film-festival |access-date=September 27, 2026 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref>

Reservations focused on structure and tone. Kate Rife of ''[[Inverse (website)|Inverse]]'' called the film a worthy follow-up and a major spectacle, but said the human story is less tightly organized than in ''Minus One''.<ref name=":22">{{Cite web |last=Rife |first=Kate |date=September 27, 2026 |title=''Godzilla Minus Zero'' Review: A Worthy Followup To The Best Godzilla Movie Of The Decade |url=https://www.inverse.com/entertainment/godzilla-minus-zero-review |access-date=September 27, 2026 |website=Inverse |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260927014114/https://www.inverse.com/entertainment/godzilla-minus-zero-review |archive-date=September 27, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> William Bibbiani of ''[[TheWrap]]'' judged it one of the stronger ''Godzilla'' sequels without ranking it among the franchise's best films, arguing that the later passages become sillier and that the drama relies more on contrivance.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bibbiani |first=William |date=September 27, 2026 |title=''Godzilla Minus Zero'' Review: One of the Great Godzilla Sequels, but Not One of the Great Godzilla Films |url=https://www.thewrap.com/creative-content/reviews/godzilla-minus-zero-review/ |access-date=September 27, 2026 |website=TheWrap |language=en-US |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260929123342/https://www.thewrap.com/creative-content/reviews/godzilla-minus-zero-review/ |archive-date=September 29, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> James Mottram, reviewing for the ''[[South China Morning Post]]'', praised the imagery and surprises while finding the ending weaker.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mottram |first=James |date=September 27, 2026 |title=Review {{!}} Godzilla Minus Zero: Japanese monster sequel an action-packed visual marvel |url=https://www.scmp.com/lifestyle/entertainment/article/3368758/godzilla-minus-zero-review-visually-stunning-japanese-monster-sequel-full-surprises |access-date=September 27, 2026 |website=South China Morning Post |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260927015104/https://www.scmp.com/lifestyle/entertainment/article/3368758/godzilla-minus-zero-review-visually-stunning-japanese-monster-sequel-full-surprises |archive-date=September 27, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>

